    "conversion_check": {
      "description": "For valid demonstrated targets, encode uses inverse(chunk reference) times commanded FK TCP and decode recomposes the same world pose. The independent check compares FK position in metres, rotation angle in radians and unchanged gripper scalar. Robust Gram-Schmidt is identity on valid 6D labels and only projects invalid/noisy sampled rotation columns; shared IK may choose a nonunique joint posture and reports convergence, residuals and limit contacts.",
      "mode": "task_space",
      "tolerance": 0.005
    },
    "cut_relation": "One model owns every action in [0, stop) of all twelve complete demonstrations. There are no cuts, segments, object choices, stage labels, runtime high-level calls or successor policies; the full-task relational reference is recomputed causally once per execution chunk.",
