      "target_pose",
      "tcp_pose"
    ],
    "output_semantics": "Each of 16 slots represents t-1 through t+14. Slots 1 through 8 execute current t through t+7. A slot is [p_ref_tcp(3 metres), R_ref_tcp first-two-columns(6), gripper(1)]. The pose is relative to the causal SE(3) reference fixed when the chunk is built. The 6D rotation is projected by robust Gram-Schmidt, composed with that reference into a world TCP target, and passed with freshly measured qpos to panda_kinematics.solve_ik. The returned seven absolute Panda joint targets are followed by the unchanged demonstrated gripper scalar; the common executor applies its >=0 open and <0 close rule. Training targets are FK poses of demonstrated native joint commands, not measured lagging TCP poses. The framework alone fits midpoint/half-range normalization in these ten represented coordinates.",
    "parameter_semantics": "There are no caller-selected parameters: call_args is exactly {} for every complete demonstration and deployment call. At each 8-step replan the policy resolves the currently observed world poses of the lid, peg, insertion target and hole. Positions are metres in the world frame and quaternions are wxyz. A causal geometric relevance blend defines one chunk-fixed SE(3) reference from the lid while closed or held at its handle, the peg while it is approached or lifted, and target_pose once lift or source-to-destination progress indicates transport. This is representation conditioning, not a stage argument or policy selector.",
